  "$comment": "Single source of truth for supported input formats. Consumed by the Python converter service (app/conversion/registry.py) and the Next.js web app (lib/formats.ts). Signature entries are byte-prefix checks; ALL entries listed for a format must match. An empty signature list means the format is text-based and must be validated by parsing instead. NOTE: .doc and .ppt are deliberately absent. markitdown 0.1.7 provides XlsConverter for legacy .xls but has no converter for legacy binary Word or PowerPoint, so they are rejected up front with a helpful message (see app/security/detection.py) rather than failing after upload.",
